# Copy to .env and fill in values.
#
# Every variable is explained with WHY it exists, not just its name — you
# should be able to set this up correctly without reading the source.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# As of M0 the app needs no environment variables at all.
#
# That is a deliberate property, not an oversight: the app is local-first, so
# it runs entirely against IndexedDB with no backend, no account, and no
# network. Nothing to configure means nothing to get wrong on a second machine.
#
# Accounts and cloud sync arrive in M5, at which point this file gains the
# Supabase project URL and anon key. Both are publishable values (the anon key
# is designed to ship in client bundles and is protected by row-level
# security), so they will live here as real examples rather than secrets —
# but they still belong in .env so the two development machines can point at
# different Supabase projects.
#
# Anything genuinely secret — a service-role key, for instance — must never
# reach this file or the client bundle. Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed
# variable into the built JavaScript, where anyone can read it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
